{'symbol': 'BR', 'date': '2022-02-01 07:00:00', 'title': 'BROADRIDGE REPORTS SECOND QUARTER FISCAL 2022 RESULTS', 'text': 'NEW YORK, FEB. 1, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0BROADRIDGE FINANCIAL SOLUTIONS, INC. (NYSE:BR) TODAY REPORTED FINANCIAL RESULTS FOR THE SECOND QUARTER ENDED DECEMBER 31, 2021 OF ITS FISCAL YEAR 2022. RESULTS COMPARED WITH THE SAME PERIOD LAST YEAR WERE AS FOLLOWS: \xa0 SUMMARY FINANCIAL RESULTS SECOND QUARTER SIX MONTHS DOLLARS IN MILLIONS, EXCEPT PER SHARE DATA 2022 2021 CHANGE 2022 2021 CHANGE RECURRING FEE REVENUES $798 $673 19% $1,548 $1,322 17% TOTAL REVENUES $1,260 $1,055 19% $2,452 $2,072 18% OPERATING INCOME 69 79 (13%) 172 158 9% \xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0 MARGIN 5.5% 7.5% 7.0% 7.6% ADJUSTED OPERATING INCOME - NON-GAAP 141 119 19% 318 269 18% \xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0 MARGIN 11.2% 11.2% 12.9% 13.0% DILUTED EPS $0.40 $0.48 (17%) $0.97 $1.04 (7%) ADJUSTED EPS - NON-GAAP $0.82 $0.73 12% $1.89 $1.70 11% CLOSED SALES $83 $44 87% $113 $76 48% "BROADRIDGE DELIVERED ANOTHER STRONG QUARTER, WITH 19% RECURRING FEE REVENUES GROWTH AND 12% GROWTH IN ADJUSTED EPS," SAID TIM GOKEY, BROADRIDGE\'S CEO.'}